---
import LegalPage from '~/components/layout/LegalPage.astro';
import { defaultLocale } from '~/i18n/routing';
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { contactEmail } from '~/lib/contact-email';
import { getUi } from '~/i18n/ui';

const email = contactEmail();
---

<LegalPage
  locale={defaultLocale}
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Rarest Answer: localStorage stats, no account, Wikidata and Wikipedia data, and optional analytics, ads, and comments."
  lastUpdated="2026-11-14"
>
  <p>
    This privacy policy describes how {site.game.name} ("we", "us", or "our") handles information
    when you visit this website. {site.game.name} is a free trivia game you play in the browser.
  </p>
  <h2>No account</h2>
  <p>
    You do not create an account. The site does not ask for a name, email address, or password to
    play or to read the guides. Streak and round stats stay in localStorage on this device. The
    game does not upload those stats to a {site.game.name} server. Answer checking runs in the
    browser against prompt data this site publishes. Clearing site data clears the stats. A
    different browser does not have them.
  </p>
  <h2>What this browser stores</h2>
  <p>localStorage on this device may hold:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Game streak and round stats.</li>
    <li>Theme choice (key <code>theme</code>).</li>
    <li>
      Cookie-consent choice (key <code>aw-cookie-consent</code>, value <code>accepted</code> or
      <code>declined</code>).
    </li>
    <li>Dismissed ad or banner flags, when an ad unit is enabled and you close it.</li>
    <li>
      A per-page "was this helpful" flag on guide pages (key <code>aw-feedback-</code> plus the
      page path).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    That storage stays on the device. It is not an account. If the browser blocks storage, the
    game can still be played, and a saved streak will not persist.
  </p>
  <h2>Wikidata and Wikipedia</h2>
  <p>
    Prompt lists are compiled from
    <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing">Wikidata</a> (CC0) and
    <a href="https://wikitech.wikimedia.org/wiki/Analytics/AQS/Pageviews">Wikipedia pageview counts</a>.
    The dataset is built ahead of time and published by this site. Playing a round does not send
    your browser to Wikidata or to the pageviews API. We use pageview counts as a popularity
    signal. We do not republish Wikipedia article text.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each prompt's <code>source</code> field names the dataset behind it. The published prompts use
    Wikidata with English Wikipedia pageviews, or Wiktionary pageviews for the English interjection
    list. A file marked <code>source: fixture</code> would still be placeholder numbers. None of the
    published prompts use that label.
  </p>
  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Paid or affiliate links may appear and are marked "{getUi(defaultLocale).houseAds.sponsored}".
  </p>
  <p>
    Advertising, analytics, and comments are off unless the matching environment variables are
    set. This site currently uses one of them: Plausible Analytics, described first below. The
    AdSense, Adsterra, Google Analytics, Cloudflare Web Analytics, VibeCafé, and giscus identifiers
    are blank, so they do not load. If they are enabled later, the services below can collect
    information under their own policies.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> (in use) — counts page views and referrers so we can see
      which pages people read. It sets no cookies, does not store your IP address, and reports only
      aggregate numbers, so it does not wait for the cookie banner. See
      <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" rel="noopener">Plausible's data policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising partners</strong> (e.g. Google AdSense, Adsterra) — may use cookies to
      serve ads. AdSense and Adsterra units load only after you accept the cookie banner, and only
      when the slot variables are set. You can refuse the banner. You can also limit ad
      personalization in the browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics</strong> (e.g. Google Analytics, Cloudflare Web Analytics, VibeCafé) —
      Google Analytics may collect usage data such as page views and approximate location. It is
      cookie-based and loads only after you accept the consent banner, and only when
      <code>PUBLIC_GA_ID</code> is set. Cloudflare Web Analytics is cookieless, does not wait for
      the banner, and loads only when <code>PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN</code> is set. VibeCafé is
      optional product telemetry. It loads only when both <code>PUBLIC_VIBECAFE_PRODUCT_ID</code>
      and <code>PUBLIC_VIBECAFE_AUTH_KEY</code> are set, and it does not wait for the banner.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — the host. Cloudflare may process request data for security and
      performance, and serves Web Analytics when that token is set.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Comments</strong> (giscus, opt-in) — the comment block renders only when the giscus
      environment variables are set. When it is on, giscus.app loads an embedded GitHub view.
      Viewing it exposes your IP address and browser information to that service. Signing in to
      comment is handled by GitHub under GitHub's privacy policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Embedded videos</strong> (YouTube) — a page that includes a video loads a thumbnail
      from i.ytimg.com and, after you press play, the player from youtube-nocookie.com. Until you
      press play, that player does not set YouTube cookies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The game itself does not use an account cookie. Third-party services listed above set cookies
    only when they actually load. You can block cookies in the browser. Blocking them does not
    remove the guides or stop a round from running. It can stop personalized ads.
  </p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {site.game.name} is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>
  <h2>Affiliation</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalNotice} This site is not affiliated with Krillion or with any other game named here.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. The
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> has the same address.
  </p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The new text will be posted on this page with a new "Last updated"
    date.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
